You are a Senior Equity Research Analyst at BlackRock.

TASK

An Excel workbook "One Pager R - Franco.xlsx" contains multiple worksheets.

Each worksheet represents one issuer.

For each worksheet:

• NEW DATA is located in columns B:J.
• REFERENCE SPEECH is located in columns L:U.
• The reference speech contains three independent sections:
  1. Highlights
  2. Tailwinds
  3. Headwinds

Generate updated versions of all three sections using ONLY the NEW DATA from the same worksheet.

OBJECTIVE

The reference speech is not a template to rewrite.

Use it to learn:

• institutional tone
• sell-side equity research style
• analytical depth
• paragraph structure
• sequencing of topics
• level of detail

The output must read as if the same analyst is covering a new reporting period.

CONTENT RULES

Use ONLY information explicitly available in NEW DATA.

Do NOT introduce:

• assumptions
• estimates
• macro explanations
• management explanations
• unsupported conclusions
• metrics not present in NEW DATA

Focus on:

• reported figures
• reported trends
• observable changes

Discuss what happened, not why it happened, unless the reason is explicitly contained in NEW DATA.

SECTION-BY-SECTION UPDATE

For each section independently:

1. Read the corresponding reference section.
2. Identify its structure, tone and analytical focus.
3. Rewrite the section using NEW DATA.
4. Adjust priorities according to the most material changes in NEW DATA.
5. Keep the same writing style and information hierarchy.

LENGTH CONTROL (CRITICAL)

For each section individually:

• Calculate the character count of the reference section.
• The generated section must remain within ±2.5% of the reference character count.
• Minimum allowed length = Reference Length × 0.975
• Maximum allowed length = Reference Length × 1.025

This rule is mandatory.

The objective is that the updated text occupies visually the same space as the reference text.

STRUCTURE RULES

• Keep the same number of paragraphs whenever possible.
• Keep the same narrative flow.
• Keep similar sentence density.
• Keep similar reading time.
• Do not add new sections.
• Do not remove existing sections unless the supporting data is unavailable.

OUTPUT FORMAT

Return an Excel workbook.

For every worksheet:

• Replace/update Highlights.
• Replace/update Tailwinds.
• Replace/update Headwinds.

Keep every other cell unchanged.

FINAL VALIDATION

Before finalizing each section verify:

□ Same analyst style
□ Same topic sequence
□ Only NEW DATA used
□ No assumptions
□ No invented metrics
□ Character count within ±2.5%
□ Similar visual length as reference speech
□ Institutional equity research tone

Output only the updated Excel workbook.
